---
// "Build once. Quote anywhere, forever." — the three-step story + code sample.
const py = `from costql import PricingPack

pack = PricingPack.load("tmdb_t3.json")          # one static file
quote = pack.quote('{ movie(id:"27205"){ cast(limit:8){ person{ name } } } }')

quote["price"]         # 50.5  — safe billable ceiling (work-ms, never dollars)
quote["typical_price"] # 36.4  — fair average estimate
quote["confidence"]    # "high" — cyclic queries come back "low", flagged not billed`;
---

<section id="build" class="cql-container cql-section">
  <h2 class="cql-h2">Build once. Quote anywhere, forever.</h2>
  <p class="cql-lead">
    Three steps from a live endpoint to a static pricing pack your app vendors like an asset.
  </p>

  <div class="cql-steps__grid">
    <div class="cql-card cql-step">
      <div class="cql-step__head">
        <span class="cql-stepnum">1</span>
        <h3>Adapt</h3>
      </div>
      <p>
        Write a ~90-line adapter: where the API is, real IDs to query with, and clean
        calibration shapes. Three worked examples ship in the repo.
      </p>
      <a href="/docs/adapters/">The adapter guide →</a>
    </div>

    <div class="cql-card cql-step">
      <div class="cql-step__head">
        <span class="cql-stepnum">2</span>
        <h3>Build</h3>
      </div>
      <p>
        <code>costql build</code> introspects the endpoint, measures calibration queries,
        fits per-resolver costs, and writes the pack.
      </p>
      <span class="cql-badge">schema + rates + fees → one JSON</span>
    </div>

    <div class="cql-card cql-step">
      <div class="cql-step__head">
        <span class="cql-stepnum">3</span>
        <h3>Quote</h3>
      </div>
      <p>
        Load the pack in Python or JavaScript and price queries locally — the JS port is
        conformance-tested to reproduce the Python engine exactly.
      </p>
      <a href="/docs/js/">How that's guaranteed →</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 24px">
    <div class="cql-code">
      <div class="cql-code__head">
        <div class="cql-dots">
          <span class="cql-dot cql-dot--aqua"></span>
          <span class="cql-dot"></span>
          <span class="cql-dot"></span>
        </div>
        <span class="cql-code__title">python</span>
      </div>
      <pre>{py}</pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
